<title>ZIMBABWE: IFC changes composition of Zimbabwe share indices.</title>
<headline>IFC changes composition of Zimbabwe share indices.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Finance Corporation (IFC) has changed the composition of its main and secondary indices for Zimbabwe with effect from November 1, brokers said on Friday.</p>
<p>On its main index -- a sample of the southern African country's five most investible stocks -- the IFC has deleted Falcon Gold and added Wankie Colliery, a move the brokers said was likely to increase investor interest in the colliery, drawing it away from the gold mining house.</p>
<p>The main index would therefore remain with five stocks comprising bankers Barclays, nickel producer Bindura, local conglomerate Delta, Wankie and hotel chain Zimbabwe Sun.</p>
<p>On its secondary index, the IFC has deleted paper products manufacturer Art and tissue mill KCI. It added clothing retailer Edgars.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
